<title>HONG KONG: Shanghai Int'l 1995/96 net jumps sharply.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Int'l 1995/96 net jumps sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 6.09	vs 0.20</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  2.0	 vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	1.57 loss vs 6.43 loss</p>
<p>    Net			  20.30     vs 0.71</p>
<p>    Turnover		   389.57    vs 394.21</p>
<p>    Company name	     Shanghai International (H.K.) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		November 1-8</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 December 6</p>
<p>NOTE - Shanghai International is a property investment, share custodian and financial services company.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on expenses incurred for early termination of operating leases for land and buildings.</p>
<p>The group has decided to change the financial year end date to December 31 from June 30 with effect from the next financial year to coincide with the financial year end date of the major shareholder, Shenyin &amp; Wanguo Securities Co Ltd. The company's next annoual report will be made in respect of the six-month period to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is two H.K. cents vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
